window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-7c8e52e0c73fc7d7"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"get-started-with-your-dot\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"dot\">开始使用 dot（专属智能体）</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>你可以在 ChatGPT 移动应用、桌面应用或桌面浏览器中创建 dot，并让它同时持续跟进多项工作。</p> <p><a id=\"create-your-dot\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"dot_1\">创建 dot</h2> <ol> <li>在 ChatGPT 移动应用、桌面应用或桌面浏览器中打开 dots，并按照介绍完成操作。</li> <li>为 dot 命名并自定义外观。你也可以保留默认设置，之后再更改。</li> <li>通过插件连接你想让 dot 使用的应用，例如电子邮件、日历和文件服务。也可以先跳过，稍后再添加。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"set-up-on-mobile-or-desktop\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_1\">在移动端或桌面端设置</h3> <p>选择最适合你的设备：ChatGPT 移动应用、桌面应用或桌面浏览器。设置完成后，你可以跨设备继续与同一个 dot 协作。</p> <p>如果你想用手机设置，请使用最新版 ChatGPT 移动应用。你可以在其中为 dot 命名、自定义外观并连接插件，还可以选择让 ChatGPT 打开后直接进入 dot 的对话。移动网页版暂不支持。如果你的账户尚不能使用 dots，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b?anchor=access\">可用资格与预览限制</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-your-computer\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_2\">连接你的电脑</h3> <p>连接自己的电脑后，dot 可以在需要时使用这台电脑：处理本地文件、利用已登录浏览器中的上下文，或启动和管理你的本地 Codex 任务。dot 使用电脑期间，请保持电脑联网，并打开 ChatGPT 应用。</p> <p>这项连接是可选的。dot 拥有自己的云端电脑，无需访问你的设备也能工作。无论你是在移动端还是桌面端创建 dot，都可以在桌面应用设置过程中或稍后<a href=\"#/article/a-6e39401d1f472a38?anchor=connect-your-computer\">连接你的电脑</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-tools-and-contact-methods\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">连接工具和联系方式</h2> <p>连接 dot 所需的资源：</p> <ul> <li><strong>应用：</strong> 通过<a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a>连接服务，让 dot 可以使用这些服务的信息和工具。</li> <li><strong>消息渠道：</strong> 打开 dot 的个人资料，选择 <strong>添加（Add）</strong>，连接 Slack 等联系方式。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c\">给 dot 发消息</a>。</li> <li><strong>你的电脑：</strong> 在 dot 的个人资料中连接一次电脑，即可让它在今后的工作中使用本地文件、代码和应用。dot 使用电脑期间，请保持电脑联网并打开 ChatGPT 应用。</li> </ul> <p>这些连接彼此独立。连接消息渠道不会自动授予 dot 访问收件箱、其他应用或电脑的权限。dot 运行在云端，并拥有自己的电脑和浏览器；无需使用你设备的工作可以直接在那里进行。</p> <p><a id=\"your-first-conversation\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">第一次对话</h2> <p>dot 会先介绍自己，再利用可用上下文和已连接应用了解你的工作，并建议它可以提供哪些帮助。它收集上下文时，你就可以开始与它交谈。如果还需要更多信息或访问权限，它会向你询问。它能提出什么建议，取决于它实际可用的信息。</p> <p>dot 会先参考相关的 ChatGPT 记忆，并在你们协作过程中继续记录笔记。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2?anchor=context-and-memory\">任务与记忆</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"give-it-a-first-task\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"start-working-together\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">开始协作</h2> <p>可以先交代一项希望 dot 持续跟踪的工作，不要把每次对话都当成全新的请求。说明重要事项、分享相关信息源，并指出哪些决定需要你参与。内置安全措施和审批检查会与你已有的应用权限同时生效。例如：</p> <figure><figcaption>筹备异地团队活动</figcaption><blockquote><p>帮我跟进异地团队活动的筹备。请根据我分享的计划和场地邮件，跟踪各项决定、截止日期和仍未答复的问题。遇到需要我处理的事项时请提醒我，并起草建议回复供我审核。</p></blockquote></figure> <p>查看结果并补充遗漏信息。dot 可以将请求中的部分工作委派给 ChatGPT Work 或 Codex。在桌面应用中打开 dot 的个人资料，选择<a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa?anchor=review-work\">活动</a>，查看已委派的工作以及待你回应的请求。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-a-follow-up\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"keep-the-work-moving\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">持续推进工作</h2> <p>dot 可以自行决定何时跟进，也可以调用后台智能体同时处理多项工作。你可以继续与它交谈，补充上下文、调整优先级或作出决定；不必在新对话中重新开始这项工作。</p> <p>告诉 dot 应将更新发送到哪里，以及什么情况下需要打断你。如果时间安排很重要，也可以要求它按固定日程运行，并注明时区和持续时间：</p> <figure><figcaption>安排定期跟进</figcaption><blockquote><p>接下来四周，请在每个工作日 Central（中部时区）上午 9 点检查已连接的计划频道。截止日期有变化时更新我的清单。如果某个截止日期可能无法按时完成，请在 ChatGPT 中联系我，并起草一条提醒供我审核。请确认日程安排。</p></blockquote></figure> <blockquote> <p>译者注：原文只写 “Central”，没有说明具体地区；美国语境中通常指美国中部时间，请按实际使用场景确认。</p> </blockquote> <p>如果已连接的信息源支持，你还可以要求 dot 在特定事件发生时采取行动，例如 Slack 频道中出现新的错误报告时。请让它确认具体设置了什么。之后可以修改某项职责或取消重复任务。结束对话或语音通话，并不一定会停止已分派的工作。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"get-started-with-your-dot\">Get started with your dot</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Create your dot in the ChatGPT mobile app, desktop app, or a desktop browser. You can give it more than one ongoing responsibility.</p> <h2 id=\"create-your-dot\">Create your dot</h2> <ol> <li>Open dots in the ChatGPT mobile app, desktop app, or a desktop browser, and follow the introduction.</li> <li>Give your dot a name and customize its appearance. You can keep the defaults and change them later.</li> <li>Connect plugins for the apps you want your dot to use, such as email, calendar, and files. You can skip this step and add them later.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"set-up-on-mobile-or-desktop\">Set up on mobile or desktop</h3> <p>Choose whichever device works best for you: the ChatGPT mobile app, desktop app, or a desktop browser. After setup, you can continue with the same dot across devices.</p> <p>If you prefer to set up on your phone, use the latest version of the ChatGPT mobile app. You can name your dot, customize its appearance, and connect plugins there. You can also choose to have ChatGPT open directly to your dot’s conversation. Mobile web is not supported. See <a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b?anchor=access\">access and preview limits</a> if dots is not available to your account.</p> <h3 id=\"connect-your-computer\">Connect your computer</h3> <p>Connecting your own computer lets your dot work there when it’s helpful: using files on your computer, working with the context of your signed-in browser, or starting and managing your local Codex tasks. Keep your computer online with the ChatGPT app open while your dot uses it.</p> <p>This connection is optional. Your dot has its own cloud computer and can work without access to your device. You can <a href=\"#/article/a-6e39401d1f472a38?anchor=connect-your-computer\">connect your computer</a> from the desktop app during setup or later, whether you created your dot on mobile or desktop.</p> <h2 id=\"connect-tools-and-contact-methods\">Connect tools and contact methods</h2> <p>Connect what your dot needs:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Apps:</strong> Connect services through <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">plugins</a> so your dot can use their information and tools.</li> <li><strong>Messaging:</strong> Open your dot's profile and select <strong>Add</strong> to connect a contact method, such as Slack. See <a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c\">Message your dot</a>.</li> <li><strong>Your computer:</strong> Connect it once from your dot’s profile to make local files, code, and apps available for future work. Keep it online with the ChatGPT app open while your dot uses it.</li> </ul> <p>These connections are separate. Connecting a messaging channel doesn't automatically grant access to an inbox, other apps, or your computer. Your dot lives in the cloud and has its own computer and browser for work that doesn't need your device.</p> <h2 id=\"your-first-conversation\">Your first conversation</h2> <p>Your dot introduces itself and uses the context and connected apps available to it to learn about your work and suggest where it can help. You can start talking to it while it gathers that context. If it needs more information or access, it can ask. Its suggestions depend on the information available to it.</p> <p>It starts with relevant ChatGPT memory and keeps notes as you work together. See <a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2?anchor=context-and-memory\">Tasks and memory</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"give-it-a-first-task\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"start-working-together\">Start working together</h2> <p>Start with work you want your dot to keep track of, rather than treating each conversation as a fresh request. Describe what matters, share the relevant sources, and explain which decisions need your input. Built-in safeguards and approval checks apply alongside your existing app permissions. For example:</p> <figure><figcaption>An offsite to organize</figcaption><blockquote><p>Help me keep our offsite on track. Use the plan and venue emails I shared to keep track of decisions, deadlines, and unanswered questions. Let me know when something needs my attention, and draft suggested replies for my review.</p></blockquote></figure> <p>Review the result and correct missing details. Your dot can delegate parts of a request to ChatGPT Work or Codex. In the desktop app, open your dot’s profile and select <a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa?anchor=review-work\">Activity</a> to inspect delegated work and requests for input.</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-a-follow-up\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"keep-the-work-moving\">Keep the work moving</h2> <p>Your dot can decide when to follow up and use background agents to work on several things at once. Keep talking to it to add context, change priorities, or make a decision. You don’t need to restart the work in a new conversation.</p> <p>Tell it where to send updates and when to interrupt you. You can also request a fixed schedule when the timing matters. Include the time zone and duration:</p> <figure><figcaption>A scheduled check-in</figcaption><blockquote><p>Check the connected planning channel each weekday at 9 AM Central for the next four weeks. Update my checklist when a deadline changes. If a deadline is at risk, message me in ChatGPT and draft a reminder for my review. Confirm the schedule.</p></blockquote></figure> <p>Where a connected source supports it, you can also ask your dot to act when a specified event occurs, such as when a new bug report appears in a Slack channel. Ask it to confirm what it set up. You can revise a responsibility or cancel a recurring task later. Ending a conversation or voice call doesn't necessarily stop assigned work.</p>"};
